    <!-- Background limits -->
    <string name="pepe_phantom_title">Background limits</string>
    <string name="pepe_phantom_button">Why Linux apps may be killed</string>
    <string name="pepe_phantom_text">Android 12 and newer stop apps that start many background processes (the "phantom process killer"). Linux programs count as such processes, so a busy session can be killed with "signal 9".\n\nOn Android 14 and newer: Settings › System › Developer options › turn on "Disable child process restrictions".\n\nOn Android 12 and 13, from a computer with adb:\n\nadb shell "/system/bin/device_config set_sync_disabled_for_tests persistent; /system/bin/device_config put activity_manager max_phantom_processes 2147483647"\n\nAlso allow pepelauncher to run unrestricted in the battery settings.</string>
